珍娜，你知道我喜欢什么吗？

866
00:46:25.090 --> 00:46:28.470
Is that how this is still a joke with the cast?
就是这件事至今在演员们之间还是个梗？

867
00:46:28.750 --> 00:46:31.410
So a few years ago, you guys, we've talked about this before.
几年前，大家，我们之前聊过这个。

868
00:46:31.550 --> 00:46:37.550
We have a cast text thread where we will text and check in, say hello, little clips, pictures of our kids.
我们有一个演员群，会在里面聊天、问候、发小视频和孩子们的照片。

869
00:46:38.070 --> 00:46:44.510
Creed usually sings us a song at Christmas, and he'll text us, you know, him at home with his, like, elf hat on.
克里德通常会在圣诞节给我们唱歌，他会发短信给我们，戴着精灵帽在家里录视频。

870
00:46:45.250 --> 00:46:47.890
And Jenna sent a photo to all of us.
然后珍娜给我们所有人发了一张照片。

871
00:46:47.890 --> 00:46:56.370
You were on a job, and you walked into, like, a little dressing room they had for you, and there was the tiniest TV mounted on the wall.
你当时在工作，走进他们为你准备的小化妆间，墙上挂着一台极小的电视。

872
00:46:56.550 --> 00:46:59.750
Jenna, and you sent us a picture, and we all started cracking up.
珍娜，你发了那张照片，我们都笑疯了。

873
00:46:59.910 --> 00:47:00.410
Yes.
是的。

874
00:47:00.410 --> 00:47:06.670
I walked into this dressing room, and I thought to myself, you could hold this in your hand.
我走进那个化妆间时心想，这玩意儿我都能拿在手里。

875
00:47:06.670 --> 00:47:09.250
Why have they mounted it on the wall?
为什么要把它挂在墙上？

876
00:47:09.430 --> 00:47:13.470
It was so reminiscent of the dinner party episode.
这太让人想起《晚宴》那一集了。

877
00:47:13.470 --> 00:47:17.990
I was so excited to send that text, and people were loving it.
我当时特别兴奋地发了那条短信，大家都特别喜欢。

878
00:47:18.370 --> 00:47:20.310
It will never get old to me, that scene.
那一幕对我来说永远不会过时。

879
00:47:20.410 --> 00:47:22.390
I can watch it and watch it and watch it.
我可以一遍又一遍地看。

880
00:47:22.510 --> 00:47:27.450
But there are so many things in this living room that made me laugh on a second watch, Jenna.
但珍娜，二刷的时候，客厅里还有好多东西让我笑个不停。

881
00:47:27.650 --> 00:47:31.990
And I also remembered it the day we were filming, because I was seated by it.
我也记起了拍摄那天的事，因为我就坐在它旁边。

882
00:47:32.890 --> 00:47:35.830
That janky side table that Michael made.
迈克尔做的那张破烂边桌。

883
00:47:36.490 --> 00:47:38.890
It is the saddest looking table.
那是看起来最寒酸的桌子了。

884
00:47:41.110 --> 00:47:43.630
It looks like scrap wood.
看起来就像废木料。

885
00:47:43.630 --> 00:47:48.770
Like, if you got a crate of firewood, that he used the crate to make the table.
就像你买了一箱木柴，然后他用那个箱子做了张桌子。

886
00:47:49.070 --> 00:47:51.210
And the dialogue cracked me up, too.
对话也让我笑喷了。

887
00:47:51.390 --> 00:47:52.570
Jim is like, is that chestnut?
吉姆问，那是栗木吗？

888
00:47:52.690 --> 00:47:56.110
And he's like, I think it's either pine or Nordic cherry.
他说，我觉得是松木或者北欧樱桃木。

889
00:47:56.490 --> 00:47:57.310
I was like, what?
我当时心想，什么鬼？

890
00:48:00.080 --> 00:48:03.300
Angela, it's time for you to arrive at this dinner party.
安吉拉，该你参加这场晚宴了。

891
00:48:03.460 --> 00:48:05.780
Oh, Andy and Angela, here we come.
哦，安迪和安吉拉，我们来了。

892
00:48:06.080 --> 00:48:08.380
We had a fan question from Haley M.
我们有一个来自海莉·M的粉丝提问。

893
00:48:08.720 --> 00:48:14.160
Angela, are you starting to break when Michael goes in for the hug, which you refuse?
安吉拉，当迈克尔想要拥抱你，而你拒绝时，你是不是快要笑场了？

894
00:48:14.160 --> 00:48:15.140
Yes.
是的。

895
00:48:15.800 --> 00:48:16.360
Yes.
没错。

896
00:48:16.680 --> 00:48:22.600
I pretty much, like John said, the minute I walked in that room and saw everything, just
就像约翰说的，我走进那个房间看到一切的那一刻，基本上……

897
00:48:22.600 --> 00:48:26.580
the minute we started those scenes, I was already tickled.
从我们开始拍那些场景的那一刻起，我就已经被逗乐了。

898
00:48:26.800 --> 00:48:30.180
And everything from then on was just me trying not to laugh.
从那以后，我所做的一切就是努力不让自己笑出来。

899
00:48:30.180 --> 00:48:33.680
I have a fun catch at 6 minutes, 34 seconds.
我在6分34秒处发现了一个有趣的细节。

900
00:48:33.960 --> 00:48:42.320
When Andy takes off his coat, underneath his coat, he is wearing a turtleneck with a shirt
当安迪脱下外套时，外套里面他穿了一件高领毛衣和一件衬衫。

901
00:48:42.320 --> 00:48:47.140
over it and then a sweater tied around his neck.
穿在外面，脖子上还系着一件毛衣。

902
00:48:47.480 --> 00:48:48.060
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

903
00:48:48.140 --> 00:48:49.740
He's in prime preppy mode.
他完全是一副典型的预科生打扮。

904
00:48:49.940 --> 00:48:53.300
This was a bit that Gene, our writer, came up with.
这是我们的编剧吉恩想出的一个桥段。

905
00:48:53.540 --> 00:48:58.620
He just thought it would be really, really funny to have a person who has tied a sweater
他觉得让一个脖子上系着毛衣的人

906
00:48:58.620 --> 00:49:01.120
around their neck, take their coat off.
脱掉外套会非常、非常搞笑。

907
00:49:01.360 --> 00:49:03.720
Yeah, they had that ready to go underneath.
没错，他们在那下面已经准备好了。

908
00:49:04.420 --> 00:49:08.580
Well, you know, I said I would let you guys know when we had some belly hiding.
嗯，你们知道的，我说过会告诉你们我们什么时候在遮肚子。

909
00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:13.480
It's happening all through the episode, but one of my favorites is this giant bouquet of
整集里都有这种情况，但我最喜欢的一个是这束巨大的

910
00:49:13.480 --> 00:49:13.880
flowers.
鲜花。

911
00:49:14.260 --> 00:49:15.740
That was to hide my belly.
那是为了遮住我的肚子。

912
00:49:15.940 --> 00:49:16.300
Yes.
是的。

913
00:49:16.480 --> 00:49:17.720
That's how big my belly is.
我的肚子就是那么大。

914
00:49:17.880 --> 00:49:19.540
Look at that bouquet of flowers.
看看那束花。

915
00:49:20.040 --> 00:49:26.300
They had to make the bouquet that big because the point of it was for Andy to give his hostess
他们必须把花束做得那么大，因为剧情需要安迪送给女主人

916
00:49:26.300 --> 00:49:30.920
some flowers, but the reason they're so large was because they were a belly hide.
一些花，但做得那么大的原因是因为它们是用来遮肚子的。

917
00:49:31.320 --> 00:49:35.400
There's a great blooper from this as well if you guys go back and rewatch them,
这一段还有一个很棒的NG镜头，如果你们回去重看的话，

918
00:49:35.420 --> 00:49:38.620
but I have a little catch I want to point out.
但我有一个小细节想指出来。

919
00:49:38.920 --> 00:49:39.600
What is it?
是什么？

920
00:49:39.840 --> 00:49:45.440
At 6 minutes, 44 seconds, I'm standing next to Jan while Andy's doing the tuna, tuna,
在6分44秒的时候，我站在简旁边，当时安迪正在说“金枪鱼，金枪鱼，

921
00:49:45.620 --> 00:49:48.200
bet you get a lot of tuna, eat a lot of tuna, that whole bit.
打赌你一定吃了很多金枪鱼，吃了很多金枪鱼”那一整段。

922
00:49:48.620 --> 00:49:48.960
Yep.
没错。

923
00:49:48.960 --> 00:49:54.920
I just, as an actor, just my own little prep that I decided to do was I just stared at
作为演员，我当时自己做了一个小准备，我决定

924
00:49:54.920 --> 00:49:55.540
Jan's boobs.
盯着简的胸部看。

925
00:49:55.740 --> 00:49:57.320
I mean, I was eye level to them.
我是说，我的视线正好和它们平齐。

926
00:49:57.440 --> 00:49:58.060
She's in heels.
她穿着高跟鞋。

927
00:49:58.220 --> 00:49:58.960
She's taller than me.
她比我高。

928
00:49:59.100 --> 00:49:59.740
They're right there.
它们就在那儿。

929
00:49:59.860 --> 00:50:04.960
And I decided to throw her a little judgy shade, Angela Martin sass look.
于是我决定给她一个评头论足的眼神，那种安吉拉·马丁式的傲慢表情。

930
00:50:05.260 --> 00:50:09.060
And Paul Feig came up to me and was like, oh my gosh, Angela, I just caught in camera
保罗·费格走过来对我说，天哪，安吉拉，我刚才在镜头里捕捉到

931
00:50:09.060 --> 00:50:12.300
that you're giving Jan's boobs the judgy look.
你在用那种审视的眼神看简的胸部。

932
00:50:12.420 --> 00:50:14.060
He was like, you got to do that every time.
他说，你每次都得这么做。

933
00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:16.220
So I did, and it made it in the show.
所以我照做了，而且这一幕被剪进了正片里。

934
00:50:16.220 --> 00:50:20.820
And it's just one of those little moments that wasn't scripted that ends up on the screen.
这就是那种没有写在剧本里，但最终出现在屏幕上的小瞬间之一。

935
00:50:20.820 --> 00:50:22.860
And it's always fun to relive those.
重温这些时刻总是很有趣。

936
00:50:22.860 --> 00:50:26.260
But that is a big, of course, Angela would do that moment.
但这绝对是一个“安吉拉当然会这么做”的经典时刻。

937
00:50:26.500 --> 00:50:27.720
Like, of course, right?
就像，当然会这样，对吧？

938
00:50:27.880 --> 00:50:29.160
I'm so glad they caught it.
我很高兴他们捕捉到了这一幕。

939
00:50:29.440 --> 00:50:35.000
This is also when we find out, Angela, that the osabuco will not be ready for at least three
这也是我们发现的时候，安吉拉，炖牛膝至少还要

940
00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:35.400
hours.
三个小时才能做好。

941
00:50:35.420 --> 00:50:41.180
And I love Pam's line when she says, do you mean three hours from now or like three
我很喜欢帕姆说的那句台词，她说，你是说从现在起三个小时，还是说

942
00:50:41.180 --> 00:50:43.840
hours from four o'clock when you started it?
从你四点钟开始做算起的三小时？

943
00:50:43.840 --> 00:50:49.240
But Jenna, when I rewatched the scene, that is one of the lines that you say that is most
但是珍娜，当我重看这一幕时，那句台词最像

944
00:50:49.240 --> 00:50:50.920
like you in real life.
现实生活中的你。

945
00:50:51.140 --> 00:50:51.760
It is.
确实是。

946
00:50:51.980 --> 00:50:56.160
It just felt like in that moment, Jenna was saying it as your friend.
感觉在那一刻，珍娜是以你朋友的身份说出那句话的。

947
00:50:56.320 --> 00:50:57.220
I was like, that would be Jenna.
我当时想，这绝对是珍娜会说的话。

948
00:50:57.460 --> 00:50:59.540
She'd be like, no, but you planned ahead.
她会说，不对，但你明明提前计划好了。

949
00:50:59.740 --> 00:51:00.140
Surely.
肯定啊。

950
00:51:00.460 --> 00:51:05.020
If you know it takes three hours, surely you had already estimated the time that you'd be
如果你知道需要三个小时，你肯定早就预估好了你会

951
00:51:05.020 --> 00:51:05.680
serving it.
上菜了。

952
00:51:06.160 --> 00:51:10.020
I feel like that is something I could possibly say.
我觉得这话我可能也会说。

953
00:51:10.180 --> 00:51:10.600
Yes.
没错。

954
00:51:10.600 --> 00:51:12.080
In response to a hoSt.
作为对主人的回应。

955
00:51:12.260 --> 00:51:14.060
Sometimes in Spain, they eat at midnight.
在西班牙，人们有时会在午夜用餐。

956
00:51:14.380 --> 00:51:15.780
So when in Rome.
所以入乡随俗嘛。

957
00:51:16.400 --> 00:51:17.480
When in Rome.
入乡随俗。

958
00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:21.340
I guess we're going to sit around and drink some wine now.
我想我们现在得坐下来喝点酒了。

959
00:51:21.720 --> 00:51:22.900
Michael makes a toaSt.
迈克尔提议祝酒。

960
00:51:23.220 --> 00:51:26.400
He notes the oaky afterbirth of the wine.
他提到了酒里那股橡木味的余韵。

961
00:51:26.880 --> 00:51:29.580
Jean told me that Steve improvised that line.
珍告诉我那句台词是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

962
00:51:29.760 --> 00:51:30.480
You're kidding.
开玩笑吧。

963
00:51:31.220 --> 00:51:32.240
Oaky afterbirth.
橡木味的余韵。

964
00:51:32.400 --> 00:51:33.160
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

965
00:51:33.420 --> 00:51:34.320
Steve Carell.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

966
00:51:34.720 --> 00:51:38.260
Well, now Jan needs to relax.
好吧，现在简需要放松一下。

967
00:51:38.660 --> 00:51:40.420
She wants to put some music on.
她想放点音乐。

968
00:51:40.600 --> 00:51:41.140
Yeah.
是啊。

969
00:51:41.480 --> 00:51:48.240
And I don't know if you know this, but her former assistant, Hunter, is a fabulous musician.
我不知道你知不知道，但她以前的助理亨特是个很棒的音乐人。

970
00:51:48.620 --> 00:51:51.180
And so she's going to put on his CD.
所以她打算放他的CD。

971
00:51:51.360 --> 00:51:52.300
It's called The Hunted.
名字叫《被猎杀者》。

972
00:51:53.000 --> 00:51:53.320
Yeah.
是啊。

973
00:51:53.480 --> 00:51:57.420
And then she's going to dance by herself in front of all of us.
然后她要在我们所有人面前独自跳舞。

974
00:51:59.420 --> 00:52:01.660
We got some fan mail about that.
我们收到了一些关于那段戏的粉丝来信。

975
00:52:01.900 --> 00:52:04.840
Amanda B., Ileana B., and Gabe G.
阿曼达·B、伊莱亚娜·B和盖比·G。

976
00:52:05.120 --> 00:52:08.580
said, please tell us everything about Jan's dance.
他们说，请告诉我们关于简跳舞的所有细节。

977
00:52:09.120 --> 00:52:10.360
Well, I'll start with this.
好吧，我先从这个说起。

978
00:52:10.860 --> 00:52:16.780
Jean told me that after we did a few takes of Melora dancing on her own, he had the idea
珍告诉我，在我们拍了几遍梅洛拉独自跳舞的镜头后，他有个想法，

979
00:52:16.780 --> 00:52:19.720
that she should try to pull Jim into the dance.
就是她应该试着把吉姆拉进舞池。

980
00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:23.240
So he got her aside and he gave her that note privately.
于是他把她叫到一边，私下里给了她这个建议。

981
00:52:23.240 --> 00:52:26.060
Really, John did not know that was going to happen.
说真的，约翰当时并不知道会发生这种事。

982
00:52:26.720 --> 00:52:28.640
Melora just ran with it.
梅洛拉只是顺势而为。

983
00:52:28.860 --> 00:52:30.880
And we didn't know either.
我们当时也不知道。

984
00:52:31.560 --> 00:52:35.000
And Jenna, when I rewatched that now, knowing that, right?
还有珍娜，我现在重看那一段时，知道了这一点，对吧？

985
00:52:35.200 --> 00:52:36.640
Because Jean shared that with you.
因为珍跟你分享过。

986
00:52:36.780 --> 00:52:38.620
And then Melora talked to me about it.
然后梅洛拉也跟我聊过这件事。

987
00:52:38.740 --> 00:52:43.120
I watched our faces, not only John's, but I watched yours and mine because it was a surprise
我观察了我们的表情，不仅是约翰的，还有你和我的，因为这对我们三个人来说都是个惊喜。

988
00:52:43.120 --> 00:52:44.080
to all three of us.
对我们三个人都是。

989
00:52:44.080 --> 00:52:49.320
And you can really see a look on both of our faces of like, what, what, what, what's happening?
你真的能从我们俩脸上看到那种表情，就像是，什么，什么，什么，发生什么事了？

990
00:52:50.320 --> 00:52:51.520
It was perfect.
太完美了。

991
00:52:52.100 --> 00:52:57.320
Well, like Angela said, we did ask Melora about this, and she told us the inspiration
嗯，就像安吉拉说的，我们确实问过梅洛拉这件事，她告诉了我们她跳舞背后的灵感。

992
00:52:57.320 --> 00:52:58.360
behind her dancing.
她跳舞背后的灵感。

993
00:52:58.860 --> 00:53:06.440
One of the most fun moments to play was the dancing with John Krasinski for the song that
演起来最有趣的时刻之一就是和约翰·卡拉辛斯基一起跳那首亨特写的歌。

994
00:53:06.440 --> 00:53:07.140
Hunter had written.
亨特写的歌。

995
00:53:07.140 --> 00:53:13.880
And it just felt like such a wonderful sort of jab at Michael, you know, so passive aggressive.
那感觉就像是对迈克尔的一种绝妙的讽刺，你知道，那种被动的攻击性。

996
00:53:14.280 --> 00:53:20.220
And also I'm a dancer, so I really wanted to just be a little like off the beat.
而且我本身是学舞蹈的，所以我真的很想让自己跳得稍微有点跟不上节拍。

997
00:53:20.380 --> 00:53:25.300
I wanted to make sure that I really tried hard to just be so inappropriate, but also
我想确保我真的努力做到非常不得体，但同时，

998
00:53:25.300 --> 00:53:30.020
just like a little bit off the beat, a little drunk, kind of a little tipsy.
又要稍微有点跟不上节拍，有点醉醺醺的，有点微醺的感觉。

999
00:53:30.100 --> 00:53:34.500
And I felt like that would be even a better, you know, even a better jab to Michael because
我觉得那样对迈克尔来说会是更好的讽刺，因为，

1000
00:53:34.500 --> 00:53:37.460
Jan and Michael are like at war at that point in the episode.
在那一集里，简和迈克尔正处于交战状态。

1001
00:53:39.470 --> 00:53:41.850
I love that she's a little off the beat.
我喜欢她那种有点不按常理出牌的感觉。

1002
00:53:42.430 --> 00:53:43.230
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1003
00:53:44.030 --> 00:53:48.130
Jan just doesn't give a s***, you know?
简就是完全不在乎，你懂吧？

1004
00:53:49.150 --> 00:53:55.330
It's so like crazy to think, if you really think it through, that she would get up at
仔细想想真的很疯狂，如果你真的深思一下，她竟然会在

1005
