也许NBC没给它加长是因为他们怀恨在心，因为格雷格坚持要按原样播出。

1575
01:25:12.010 --> 01:25:12.350
Ooh.
噢。

1576
01:25:14.190 --> 01:25:14.710
Wow.
哇。

1577
01:25:14.710 --> 01:25:16.250
I love that speculation.
我喜欢这个推测。

1578
01:25:16.370 --> 01:25:21.050
They're like, no, you can have your weirdo episode, but it's only going to be 22 minutes.
他们就像是说，不行，你可以保留你那古怪的剧集，但只能有22分钟。

1579
01:25:21.070 --> 01:25:22.450
We're not going to make it big.
我们不会把它做成大制作的。

1580
01:25:23.050 --> 01:25:24.310
That's what she said.
这就是她说的。

1581
01:25:24.530 --> 01:25:26.190
Oh, that's what she said.
噢，这就是她说的。

1582
01:25:27.250 --> 01:25:33.810
One other little detail from this dinner party is how enormous the glasses were that Dwight was drinking from.
关于这场晚宴的另一个小细节是德怀特用的酒杯大得离谱。

1583
01:25:34.070 --> 01:25:36.690
To me, they look like glasses you buy at Spencer's Gifts.
对我来说，它们看起来就像你在Spencer's Gifts买的那种杯子。

1584
01:25:36.890 --> 01:25:41.270
Remember that place in the mall where you could get, like, kind of joke-sized stuff?
还记得商场里那个可以买到各种恶搞尺寸东西的地方吗？

1585
01:25:41.550 --> 01:25:46.450
Well, Paul really loved these glasses, and there was one detail about them he wanted to share with us.
嗯，保罗真的很喜欢这些杯子，关于它们，他有一个细节想和我们分享。

1586
01:25:46.990 --> 01:25:53.770
One of my favorite gags in the show is when Dwight comes over with his babysitter and they're at dinner with the wine glasses.
我最喜欢的剧集笑点之一，就是德怀特带着保姆来吃晚饭，用着那些红酒杯的时候。

1587
01:25:53.770 --> 01:26:00.870
I had them fill the wine all the way to the top because I figured that's what Dwight would think you would do with a big wine glass is you would fill it right to the rim.
我让他们把酒倒满，因为我想德怀特会觉得用大酒杯就该倒到杯沿。

1588
01:26:00.870 --> 01:26:05.110
So that's a little wine lover's joke for everybody.
所以这是给各位红酒爱好者开的一个小玩笑。

1589
01:26:05.650 --> 01:26:07.730
You know what they look like to me, Angela?
安吉拉，你知道它们让我想起什么吗？

1590
01:26:08.010 --> 01:26:14.970
They look like those wine glasses that I see a lot of moms post on Instagram about getting through their day.
它们看起来就像我在Instagram上经常看到妈妈们发的那些用来熬过一天的红酒杯。

1591
01:26:15.490 --> 01:26:19.570
Wine weekend with the ladies and the wine glasses like the size of your head.
和闺蜜们的红酒周末，酒杯大得像脑袋一样。

1592
01:26:19.790 --> 01:26:20.230
Yes.
没错。

1593
01:26:20.530 --> 01:26:22.030
That's what they remind me of.
它们让我想到的就是那个。

1594
01:26:22.250 --> 01:26:22.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1595
01:26:22.810 --> 01:26:23.790
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1596
01:26:23.990 --> 01:26:24.790
Lady, guess what?
女士，猜猜怎么着？

1597
01:26:24.990 --> 01:26:25.290
What?
什么？

1598
01:26:25.290 --> 01:26:26.810
The food is ready.
饭做好了。

1599
01:26:27.170 --> 01:26:29.590
The food is ready, but it might be poisoned.
饭做好了，但可能被下毒了。

1600
01:26:30.010 --> 01:26:30.850
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1601
01:26:31.330 --> 01:26:32.410
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1602
01:26:32.490 --> 01:26:32.790
Yes.
是的。

1603
01:26:32.950 --> 01:26:34.290
Michael whispers to Pam.
迈克尔在跟帕姆耳语。

1604
01:26:34.610 --> 01:26:38.930
He thinks that Jan has maybe been trying to poison him.
他觉得简可能一直在试图给他下毒。

1605
01:26:39.070 --> 01:26:41.090
He can't prove it, but he thinks.
他没法证明，但他就是这么想的。

1606
01:26:41.410 --> 01:26:44.170
He just hopes she didn't do anything to the food tonight.
他只希望简今晚没在食物里动什么手脚。

1607
01:26:44.530 --> 01:26:45.990
Like, what has been happening to Michael?
话说，迈克尔到底怎么了？

1608
01:26:46.110 --> 01:26:47.670
Has he been having violent diarrhea?
他是有剧烈腹泻吗？

1609
01:26:48.170 --> 01:26:50.550
Stomach cramping after he eats with her?
还是跟她吃完饭后胃绞痛？

1610
01:26:50.770 --> 01:26:52.830
Like, what is making him think this?
到底是什么让他这么想？

1611
01:26:53.430 --> 01:26:54.910
Pam has a talking head.
帕姆在接受采访。

1612
01:26:55.190 --> 01:26:56.770
Poor Pam is so hungry.
可怜的帕姆饿坏了。

1613
01:26:57.050 --> 01:27:00.450
She says she knows that Jan did not poison the food.
她说她知道简没在食物里下毒。

1614
01:27:00.690 --> 01:27:08.590
But if she were going to poison the food, wouldn't she have poisoned Pam since she is Michael's former lover?
但如果简真要下毒，难道不该连帕姆一起毒死吗？毕竟帕姆是迈克尔的前任情人。

1615
01:27:09.530 --> 01:27:12.570
And now you know Pam is not going to be able to eat.
现在你知道帕姆肯定吃不下饭了。

1616
01:27:12.850 --> 01:27:14.990
You guys, Michael has soft teeth.
伙计们，迈克尔的牙齿很软。

1617
01:27:15.410 --> 01:27:16.950
We learned that in this episode.
我们是在这一集里知道的。

1618
01:27:17.430 --> 01:27:23.750
And because of his soft teeth, he has to dip his meat into his wine or probably whatever beverage is in front of him.
因为牙齿软，他得把肉蘸进红酒里，或者蘸进他面前的任何饮料里。

1619
01:27:24.010 --> 01:27:26.350
And Jan hates it.
而简对此深恶痛绝。

1620
01:27:26.730 --> 01:27:28.890
This has clearly come up before.
这事儿显然以前就发生过。

1621
01:27:29.310 --> 01:27:30.690
And she doesn't want him to do it.
她不想让他这么做。

1622
01:27:30.750 --> 01:27:31.870
She's like, could you stop doing it?
她就像是在说，你能别这样吗？

1623
01:27:31.970 --> 01:27:32.790
It's disgusting.
太恶心了。

1624
01:27:33.630 --> 01:27:36.230
Lady, can I tell you a story about a guy I dated?
女士，我能给你讲讲我以前约会过的一个男人的故事吗？

1625
01:27:36.470 --> 01:27:36.930
Oh, God.
天哪。

1626
01:27:36.930 --> 01:27:40.470
I was so worried you were about to tell me you dipped meat into your beverages.
我刚才真担心你要说你也会把肉蘸进饮料里。

1627
01:27:40.470 --> 01:27:41.670
But it's about a different.
但那是关于另一个人的。

1628
01:27:41.850 --> 01:27:42.310
It's a guy.
是个男的。

1629
01:27:42.850 --> 01:27:45.370
Angela, how long have you known me?
安吉拉，你认识我多久了？

1630
01:27:45.370 --> 01:27:49.870
You thought maybe I dip my meat in beverages?
你竟然以为我会把肉蘸进饮料里？

1631
01:27:50.110 --> 01:27:51.590
Well, you made a face.
好吧，你刚才做了个表情。

1632
01:27:51.590 --> 01:27:53.050
You guys can't see her.
你们看不到她。

1633
01:27:53.150 --> 01:27:54.750
But she made a face.
但她确实做了个表情。

1634
01:27:54.970 --> 01:28:00.470
You did the thing with your shoulders that you do, Jenna, when you're about to share something with me that you haven't shared before.
珍娜，你刚才耸了耸肩，就是你准备跟我分享什么从未说过的事情时会有的那种动作。

1635
01:28:00.710 --> 01:28:02.410
And so I thought, oh, my God.
所以我当时想，天哪。

1636
01:28:02.850 --> 01:28:05.370
I've eaten with her, but have I ever eaten red meat with her?
我跟她一起吃过饭，但我跟她一起吃过红肉吗？

1637
01:28:05.510 --> 01:28:06.030
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1638
01:28:06.630 --> 01:28:08.550
No, I eat meat normally.
不，我吃肉的方式很正常。

1639
01:28:08.710 --> 01:28:11.370
I can't believe that's a sentence I had to say.
真不敢相信我竟然得说出这种话。

1640
01:28:11.570 --> 01:28:11.970
Well.
好吧。

1641
01:28:12.190 --> 01:28:12.910
But I did.
但我确实说了。

1642
01:28:13.190 --> 01:28:13.630
No.
不。

1643
01:28:13.630 --> 01:28:21.230
So what I was going to share was I dated a guy who, first of all, had to drink milk with every meal, not water.
我要分享的是，我曾和一个男的约会，首先，他每顿饭都必须喝牛奶，而不是水。

1644
01:28:21.610 --> 01:28:25.190
He is a grown man, but he had to have a big, tall glass of milk.
他是个成年男人，却非得喝一大杯牛奶。

1645
01:28:25.370 --> 01:28:29.330
I mean, maybe no judgment, but I'm just saying, I don't know.
我是说，也许不该评判别人，但我只是想说，我不知道。

1646
01:28:29.590 --> 01:28:30.210
I judge.
我会评判。

1647
01:28:30.430 --> 01:28:31.130
Okay, go on.
好吧，继续说。

1648
01:28:31.690 --> 01:28:32.650
We're at a restaurant.
我们在餐厅里。

1649
01:28:32.870 --> 01:28:34.230
Orders a tall glass of milk.
他点了一大杯牛奶。

1650
01:28:35.070 --> 01:28:48.610
But he had this thing where he would take a bite of food and then immediately take a sip of milk and then chew the food with the milk in his mouth and then swallow it.
但他有个怪癖，他会咬一口食物，然后立刻喝一口牛奶，接着把食物和牛奶含在嘴里一起嚼，然后再咽下去。

1651
01:28:48.630 --> 01:28:50.350
Oh, God.
天哪。

1652
01:28:50.530 --> 01:28:54.170
And you had to sit and watch that through a whole meal?
你居然得坐在那儿看他吃完一整顿饭？

1653
01:28:54.170 --> 01:28:58.250
Well, this was his preferred way of eating.
嗯，这是他偏好的进食方式。

1654
01:28:58.530 --> 01:29:03.230
He liked the taste of his food mixed with a sip of milk.
他喜欢把食物和一口牛奶混在一起吃。

1655
01:29:03.610 --> 01:29:04.950
All foods?
所有食物都这样？

1656
01:29:05.810 --> 01:29:08.230
That's every meal, every food.
每一顿饭，每一种食物都这样。

1657
01:29:08.410 --> 01:29:10.130
A bite of sandwich, sip of milk.
咬一口三明治，喝一口牛奶。

1658
01:29:10.610 --> 01:29:12.750
A fork full of spaghetti, sip of milk.
叉起一叉意面，喝一口牛奶。

1659
01:29:12.970 --> 01:29:14.250
That is disgusting.
那太恶心了。

1660
01:29:15.390 --> 01:29:16.850
That's a deal breaker for me.
这对我来说绝对无法接受。

1661
01:29:16.950 --> 01:29:23.410
I can't spend the rest of my life watching you take one bite, a swig of milk, and slosh it around.
我可没法余生都看着你吃一口饭，喝一口奶，还在嘴里搅来搅去。

1662
01:29:23.530 --> 01:29:24.150
I can't do it.
我做不到。

1663
01:29:24.210 --> 01:29:24.490
I'm out.
我不干了。

1664
01:29:24.790 --> 01:29:26.330
I dated him a long time.
我和他交往了很久。

1665
01:29:26.490 --> 01:29:27.210
How long?
多久？

1666
01:29:27.730 --> 01:29:28.790
I don't want to say.
我不想说。

1667
01:29:28.910 --> 01:29:29.490
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1668
01:29:30.370 --> 01:29:31.210
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1669
01:29:31.350 --> 01:29:32.470
But it was a lot of meals.
但那确实吃了很多顿饭。

1670
01:29:32.730 --> 01:29:34.390
A lot of milk meals.
很多顿牛奶饭。

1671
01:29:34.830 --> 01:29:35.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1672
01:29:35.770 --> 01:29:42.990
Well, listen, Michael is really offended that Jan has pointed out this quirk in front of the dinner party.
听着，迈克尔真的很生气，因为简在晚宴上当众指出了这个怪癖。

1673
01:29:43.450 --> 01:29:45.650
And she is so evil.
而且她太坏了。

1674
01:29:45.650 --> 01:29:47.510
She goes, oops.
她居然说，哎呀。

1675
01:29:48.070 --> 01:29:49.030
And that's it.
就这么一句。

1676
01:29:49.190 --> 01:29:50.190
Michael has had it.
迈克尔忍无可忍了。

1677
01:29:50.490 --> 01:29:52.970
He is going to take back his space.
他要夺回自己的主场。

1678
01:29:53.250 --> 01:29:54.630
He marches off.
他大步走开了。

1679
01:29:54.750 --> 01:29:56.690
We don't know where he's going or what he's getting.
我们不知道他要去哪儿，也不知道他要拿什么。

1680
01:29:57.250 --> 01:30:01.290
While he's gone, I got a little glimpse of your plate, Angela.
在他离开的时候，我瞥了一眼你的盘子，安吉拉。

1681
01:30:01.950 --> 01:30:02.310
Yeah?
是吗？

1682
01:30:02.610 --> 01:30:04.830
Will you please tell people what you did?
你能告诉大家你做了什么吗？

1683
01:30:05.070 --> 01:30:07.930
You guys, it was one of those little actory moments.
伙计们，那只是那种演员式的小动作。

1684
01:30:07.930 --> 01:30:13.130
And it might also have been because I was really pregnant and everything was smelling so strong to me.
而且可能也是因为我当时怀孕了，对气味特别敏感。

1685
01:30:13.290 --> 01:30:18.250
But I took my napkin, my fancy napkin that Jan had laid out for all of us,
但我拿起了餐巾，就是简为我们每个人准备的那种精致餐巾，

1686
01:30:18.350 --> 01:30:23.330
and I just gently covered my meat with it so I didn't have to look at it.
然后轻轻地盖住了我的肉，这样我就不用看着它了。

1687
01:30:23.530 --> 01:30:26.750
And I thought Angela Martin would do that because she's a vegetarian.
我当时想，安吉拉·马丁会这么做，因为她是素食主义者。

1688
01:30:26.750 --> 01:30:29.590
She wouldn't have eaten the meat or wanted to look at it.
她肯定不会吃那块肉，也不想看着它。

1689
01:30:29.690 --> 01:30:35.610
But she wasn't going to say anything because this is clearly not the dinner party where you want to voice up about the food.
但她又不敢说什么，因为这显然不是那种可以对食物提出异议的晚宴。

1690
01:30:35.970 --> 01:30:38.410
So I covered my meat with the napkin.
所以我用餐巾盖住了肉。

1691
01:30:38.690 --> 01:30:39.450
So brilliant.
太聪明了。

1692
01:30:39.850 --> 01:30:40.890
I love that choice.
我喜欢这个选择。

1693
01:30:41.470 --> 01:30:47.950
Well, Michael comes back to the table and he has brought with him his neon beer sign.
迈克尔回到桌边，带回了他的霓虹灯啤酒招牌。

1694
01:30:47.950 --> 01:30:52.370
And he takes a painting off the wall, which, by the way, I want to point out is red.
他把墙上的一幅画取了下来，顺便提一下，那幅画是红色的。

1695
01:30:52.610 --> 01:30:53.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1696
01:30:53.270 --> 01:30:55.110
And he hangs up his beer sign.
然后他挂上了他的啤酒招牌。

1697
01:30:55.390 --> 01:30:59.210
And when the neon light goes on, you hear the hum.
当霓虹灯亮起时，你能听到嗡嗡声。

1698
01:30:59.210 --> 01:31:04.190
And we are just bathed in this glow from this sign.
我们都被这招牌发出的光笼罩着。

1699
01:31:04.390 --> 01:31:10.330
Well, listen, it's a St. Polly girl beer sign, and it's outlined in blue.
听着，那是个圣保利女孩啤酒招牌，轮廓是蓝色的。

1700
01:31:10.610 --> 01:31:17.150
So when he turned it on, it was like a cascade of blue light filled the whole room.
所以当他打开开关时，就像一股蓝色的光瀑布填满了整个房间。

1701
01:31:17.390 --> 01:31:18.830
It's just so incredible.
这真是太不可思议了。

1702
01:31:18.830 --> 01:31:21.850
And you see the blue on Melora's face.
你可以看到梅洛拉脸上的蓝色光影。

1703
01:31:22.050 --> 01:31:23.730
That's how bright the light is.
那是因为灯光太亮了。

1704
01:31:24.490 --> 01:31:26.470
Jan is furious.
简非常愤怒。

1705
01:31:27.230 --> 01:31:28.250
She gets up.
她站了起来。

1706
01:31:28.370 --> 01:31:30.270
She turns on Hunter's CD.
她打开了亨特的CD。

1707
01:31:30.570 --> 01:31:34.070
And now we are going to have the argument.
现在我们要迎来那场争吵了。

1708
01:31:34.550 --> 01:31:35.070
Yeah.
没错。

1709
01:31:35.250 --> 01:31:39.290
We thought we had the argument, but now the showdown is about to happen.
我们以为争吵已经结束了，但真正的对决才刚刚开始。

1710
01:31:39.590 --> 01:31:40.190
Yeah.
没错。

1711
01:31:40.190 --> 01:31:45.050
They start arguing about talent, about creativity.
他们开始争论起才华和创造力的问题。

1712
01:31:45.870 --> 01:31:48.670
Michael's like, I don't think he's a good singer.
迈克尔觉得，我不认为他是个好歌手。

1713
01:31:48.670 --> 01:31:50.530
I don't think he's very good at all.
我觉得他一点都不好。

1714
01:31:50.630 --> 01:31:52.330
But Jan seems to love him.
但简似乎很喜欢他。

1715
01:31:52.490 --> 01:31:54.790
It's one of my favorite lines.
这是我最喜欢的台词之一。

1716
01:31:55.290 --> 01:31:57.470
Jan says, at least he's an artiSt.
简说，至少他是个艺术家。

1717
01:31:57.710 --> 01:32:01.090
And Michael says, BFD, I'm a screenwriter.
迈克尔说，那又怎样，我还是个编剧呢。

1718
01:32:01.330 --> 01:32:03.410
And this is my favorite line.
这是我最喜欢的一句台词。

1719
01:32:03.770 --> 01:32:08.890
Jan says, and I'm a candle maker, but you don't hear me bragging about it.
简说，我还是个蜡烛制作人呢，但我可没到处吹嘘。

1720
01:32:09.570 --> 01:32:12.510
Yeah, it's one of my favorite lines of the whole episode.
没错，这是整集中我最喜欢的台词之一。

1721
01:32:13.370 --> 01:32:15.050
I also like this couplet.
我也很喜欢这一对儿台词。

1722
01:32:15.370 --> 01:32:17.770
You burn it, you buy it.
点燃了就得买。

1723
01:32:17.950 --> 01:32:21.830
And then Michael says, great, I'll be your first customer.
然后迈克尔说，太好了，那我会是你的第一个顾客。

1724
01:32:22.090 --> 01:32:24.150
You're hardly my firSt.
你才不是第一个。

1725
01:32:29.330 --> 01:32:31.850
Leave, we got to sit in that room.
天哪，我们当时就坐在那个房间里。

1726
01:32:32.210 --> 01:32:32.930
I know.
我知道。

1727
01:32:33.230 --> 01:32:38.310
I mean, we got front row seats to this live show.
我是说，我们就像坐在前排看现场直播一样。

1728
01:32:38.670 --> 01:32:40.570
It was mind blowing.
简直让人大开眼界。

1729
01:32:40.570 --> 01:32:47.250
Just the two of them were doing this dance and we got to watch it.
他们俩就在那儿演着对手戏，而我们就在旁边看着。

1730
01:32:47.370 --> 01:32:50.170
I am still blown away that we got to be there.
直到现在，我依然为能亲临现场感到震撼。

1731
01:32:50.450 --> 01:32:55.750
Well, when we asked Rainn Wilson about this episode, this is what he talked about.
嗯，当我们问雷恩·威尔森关于这一集的内容时，他就是这么说的。

1732
01:32:55.750 --> 01:33:08.590
I think the true hero of Dinner Party is the magnificent Melora Hardin, who is insanely brilliant all through the series, but especially in that episode.
我觉得《晚宴》这一集的真正英雄是伟大的梅洛拉·哈丁，她在整部剧中都表现得极其出色，尤其是在这一集里。

1733
01:33:08.590 --> 01:33:22.030
I mean, Steve Carell being one of the all-time greats on the planet Earth comedic actors, and Melora Hardin stands toe-to-toe with him all the way through it, being just as funny,
我是说，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔是地球上最伟大的喜剧演员之一，而梅洛拉·哈丁在整场戏中都与他旗鼓相当，同样搞笑，

1734
01:33:22.230 --> 01:33:24.510
just as specific, just as weird.
同样精准，同样古怪。

1735
01:33:24.510 --> 01:33:37.570
And it's where you kind of see that Jan has turned a corner and that there is underneath this kind of external facade of blonde efficiency.
在这一集里，你会发现简已经彻底变了，在那层金发干练的外表之下。

1736
01:33:37.570 --> 01:33:43.770
There is a very, very weird, egotistical, messed up human being under there.
隐藏着一个非常、非常古怪、自负且扭曲的人。

1737
01:33:43.990 --> 01:33:45.930
Her candles, on and on.
还有她的蜡烛，没完没了。

1738
01:33:46.110 --> 01:33:48.670
But her performance is just magnificent.
但她的表演简直太精彩了。

1739
01:33:48.690 --> 01:33:50.030
It's so dry.
那种冷幽默感太棒了。

1740
01:33:50.370 --> 01:33:59.810
It stands the test of time as just one of the great all-time performances all throughout the series, but especially in that episode.
这绝对经得起时间的考验，是整部剧中最伟大的表演之一，尤其是在这一集里。

1741
01:33:59.990 --> 01:34:05.370
When I rewatched it recently with my son, I was blown away by how great she was.
最近我和儿子重温这一集时，我被她的演技深深折服了。

1742
01:34:06.610 --> 01:34:08.690
Melora is the star of this episode.
梅洛拉是这一集的主角。

1743
01:34:08.890 --> 01:34:09.890
She just is.
她确实是。

1744
01:34:10.370 --> 01:34:10.670
Yeah.
没错。

1745
01:34:11.070 --> 01:34:13.350
We were so lucky to have her.
我们能拥有她真是太幸运了。

1746
01:34:13.570 --> 01:34:19.410
I mean, back on the pilot when we cast her, could we have known that this is what was going to happen?
我是说，回想试播集选角的时候，我们怎么可能预见到后来会发生这些事呢？

1747
01:34:19.870 --> 01:34:29.290
Well, Jenna, Melora has shared with us that she felt like they knew the chemistry these characters could have if they really got room to run.
嗯，珍娜，梅洛拉曾告诉我们，她觉得他们当时就预感到了，如果给这些角色足够的发挥空间，他们之间会产生怎样的化学反应。

1748
01:34:29.490 --> 01:34:31.990
Way back on the pilot, here's what she had to say.
早在试播集时，她是这样说的。

1749
01:34:31.990 --> 01:34:39.110
The whole Jan and Michael arc started when we were having lunch at the pilot episode.
简和迈克尔的故事线始于我们在试播集拍摄期间的一次午餐。

1750
01:34:39.530 --> 01:34:43.270
Me and Steve and Greg were all having lunch together.
当时我和史蒂夫还有格雷格正在一起吃午饭。

1751
01:34:43.530 --> 01:34:53.610
And somehow Steve and I both said, like, there was just some spark and some weird dysfunctional attraction between Michael and Jan that if we ever got so lucky to make the series,
史蒂夫和我当时都觉得，迈克尔和简之间有一种火花，一种奇怪且功能失调的吸引力，如果我们有幸能制作这部剧，

1752
01:34:53.610 --> 01:34:58.330
we would hope that we could get them to hook up somehow, some way at some conference or something.
我们希望能让他们以某种方式，在某个会议或其他场合勾搭上。

1753
01:34:58.490 --> 01:34:59.890
So that was the beginning of it.
这就是一切的开端。

1754
01:34:59.890 --> 01:35:12.950
So I think going into it, I was always aware of what the potential for sort of showing this wonderfully complicated and dysfunctional relationship was the hilarity of that.
所以我认为在开始制作时，我就意识到展现这种极其复杂且功能失调的关系所带来的喜剧潜力。

1755
01:35:13.090 --> 01:35:21.370
It was just so funny and so kind of dark, darkly funny, which just really appeals to my personal sensibilities.
这太搞笑了，而且有一种黑暗的、黑色幽默感，这非常符合我的个人喜好。

1756
01:35:21.370 --> 01:35:28.110
I really loved that the dinner party took it to that next step of implosion.
我真的很喜欢“晚宴”那一集把这种关系推向了崩溃的边缘。

1757
01:35:28.550 --> 01:35:29.650
Yeah, I was just thrilled.
没错，我当时太激动了。

1758
01:35:29.830 --> 01:35:39.790
I was just thrilled that we had a chance to really implode on screen in front of everybody and hopefully get a lot of laughs out of it, which we did.
我很高兴我们有机会在镜头前、在所有人面前彻底爆发，并希望能从中获得很多笑声，我们确实做到了。

1759
01:35:39.790 --> 01:35:55.630
Well, speaking of implosion, this whole thing is about to crescendo when Jan picks up a Dundee and smashes Michael's beloved plasma screen TV.
说到爆发，当简拿起一个邓迪奖杯砸向迈克尔心爱的等离子电视时，整件事达到了高潮。

1760
01:35:56.830 --> 01:36:06.380
Yeah, I mean, he's like, back on your zero dollar salary, babe.
没错，他的意思是，宝贝，回到你那零美元的薪水去吧。

1761
01:36:07.640 --> 01:36:13.860
Oh, my favorite moment after that, there's the silence of like, oh, my God, what just happened?
哦，在那之后我最喜欢的时刻，是那种寂静，就像是，天哪，刚才发生了什么？

1762
01:36:13.860 --> 01:36:20.140
And the person that calls it for the night that's like, yeah, I'm done here is Melvina.
而那个决定结束这一切，说“好吧，我受够了”的人是梅尔维娜。

1763
01:36:20.560 --> 01:36:22.440
She's like, yeah, I'm going to go.
她说，好吧，我要走了。

1764
01:36:23.460 --> 01:36:26.700
Well, Melvina is the only person who doesn't work for this guy.
嗯，梅尔维娜是唯一一个不为这家伙工作的人。

1765
01:36:26.780 --> 01:36:30.480
So she could be like, yeah, I'm out of here.
所以她可以表现得，好吧，我撤了。

1766
01:36:30.780 --> 01:36:30.920
Yeah.
没错。

1767
01:36:31.180 --> 01:36:32.740
This has taken a turn for me.
对我来说，事情变得有些不对劲了。

1768
01:36:32.740 --> 01:36:37.520
Well, we had a fan question, Angela, from Meg, Emily, Ethan and Emma.
安吉拉，我们收到了梅格、艾米丽、伊森和艾玛的粉丝提问。

1769
01:36:37.800 --> 01:36:45.180
How many plasma screen TVs were broken by a Dundee and how many takes did this actually require?
一共砸坏了多少台等离子电视，实际拍摄了多少次？

1770
01:36:45.480 --> 01:36:52.220
Well, I reached out to good old Kentopedia, who told me that those little TVs were actually kind of expensive.
我咨询了老朋友肯托百科（Kentopedia），他告诉我那些小电视其实挺贵的。

1771
01:36:52.800 --> 01:36:57.620
He said they bought five of them and we broke four.
他说他们买了五台，我们砸坏了四台。

1772
01:36:58.000 --> 01:37:02.640
Oh, now I remember doing a bunch of takes with Melora where she missed.
哦，现在我想起来了，我和梅洛拉拍了很多次，她都没砸中。

1773
01:37:02.740 --> 01:37:06.480
At first, and they would have us react as if she hit it.
起初，他们会让我们表现得好像她砸中了一样。

1774
01:37:06.720 --> 01:37:09.020
They could always use our reaction.
他们总能用上我们的反应镜头。

1775
01:37:09.560 --> 01:37:16.260
But then she only had those five chances to actually land the Dundee when she was on camera.
但她只有那五次机会在镜头前真正砸中邓迪奖杯。

1776
01:37:16.520 --> 01:37:21.000
And, you know, I mean, the sort of comical thing is it wasn't a big target.
你知道，好笑的是，那并不是一个很大的目标。

1777
01:37:21.720 --> 01:37:26.420
It's a small thing to hit square in the middle with a Dundee.
用邓迪奖杯精准砸中正中心其实很难。

1778
01:37:26.720 --> 01:37:27.480
It's true.
确实。

1779
01:37:27.860 --> 01:37:30.860
Well, we're all going to follow Melvina out the door, right?
好吧，我们都要跟着梅尔维娜出门了，对吧？

1780
01:37:30.860 --> 01:37:32.400
Everyone gets up from the table.
大家都从桌边站了起来。

1781
01:37:32.760 --> 01:37:33.460
They're going to leave.
他们要离开了。

1782
01:37:33.660 --> 01:37:37.060
I was actually asked not to get up from the table, if you notice.
如果你注意看的话，其实我被要求不要从桌边站起来。

1783
01:37:37.620 --> 01:37:39.380
And it's because you would have seen my belly.
这是因为如果你站起来就会看到我的肚子。

1784
01:37:39.540 --> 01:37:42.780
So I'm the last to leave the dining room.
所以我成了最后一个离开餐厅的人。

1785
01:37:42.960 --> 01:37:46.000
Well, not only do we leave, but the police arrive.
嗯，不仅我们离开了，警察也到了。

1786
01:37:46.400 --> 01:37:49.340
There are two moments that are so delicious in the scene.
这一幕里有两个非常精彩的时刻。

1787
01:37:49.660 --> 01:37:52.900
Well, one of my first things is right away the police officers are like,
其中一个我最先注意到的就是，警察一进来就说，

1788
01:37:53.000 --> 01:37:55.920
hey, Dwight, because they know him because he's always hanging around them.
嘿，德怀特，因为他们认识他，他总是围着他们转。

1789
01:37:55.920 --> 01:37:57.520
He, like, wants to be part of the club.
他就像是想加入他们的圈子一样。

1790
01:37:58.120 --> 01:38:04.580
And the other thing is, is when Michael says to them, as if they know what he's talking about,
另一个时刻是，当迈克尔对他们说，就好像他们知道他在说什么一样，

1791
01:38:04.660 --> 01:38:08.300
he says, my girlfriend threw a Dundee at my TV.
他说，我女朋友拿邓迪奖杯砸了我的电视。

1792
01:38:08.940 --> 01:38:09.480
Yeah.
没错。

1793
01:38:09.900 --> 01:38:10.800
Can you imagine?
你能想象吗？

1794
01:38:12.830 --> 01:38:18.030
Well, they ask if he wants to press charges because some neighbors heard a lot of yelling,
他们问他是否要起诉，因为有邻居听到了很大的叫喊声，

1795
01:38:18.270 --> 01:38:19.650
a big domestic disturbance.
一场严重的家庭纠纷。

1796
01:38:20.150 --> 01:38:23.030
And Michael says, I'll take the fall.
迈克尔说，我会承担责任的。

1797
01:38:23.230 --> 01:38:28.370
And they're like, no, I, there's, you're actually, you're actually not in fault.
他们说，不，你其实，你其实并没有错。

1798
01:38:28.590 --> 01:38:30.190
You don't have to take the fall.
你不需要承担责任。

1799
01:38:30.470 --> 01:38:32.490
Is there anywhere you can go tonight?
今晚你有地方去吗？

1800
01:38:32.870 --> 01:38:33.250
Yeah.
没错。

1801
01:38:33.250 --> 01:38:36.770
And Dwight offers to take Michael home with him,
德怀特提出带迈克尔回家，

1802
01:38:37.010 --> 01:38:41.390
which Michael refuses until he sees Jan come out of the condo.
迈克尔起初拒绝了，直到他看到简从公寓里走出来。

1803
01:38:41.530 --> 01:38:42.630
And then he's like, yeah, yeah.
然后他就改口说，好啊，好啊。

1804
01:38:42.730 --> 01:38:44.050
Okay, no, I'll go home with you.
行，没问题，我跟你回家。

1805
01:38:44.510 --> 01:38:49.110
Well, Jenna, as everyone is leaving, there was a Dwight and Angela deleted scene.
珍娜，在大家离开的时候，有一段德怀特和安吉拉的删减片段。

1806
01:38:49.590 --> 01:38:53.170
And Angela is very sassy with Dwight.
安吉拉对德怀特非常傲慢无礼。

1807
01:38:53.550 --> 01:38:54.750
I want to play it.
我想放给大家看。

1808
01:38:55.410 --> 01:38:57.570
I noticed you're wearing open-toed shoes.
我注意到你穿了露趾鞋。

1809
01:38:58.770 --> 01:39:00.310
Since when did you become a whore?
你什么时候变得这么放荡了？

1810
01:39:01.590 --> 01:39:04.410
There might be a lot of things about me that shock you.
关于我，可能会有很多让你震惊的事情。

1811
01:39:05.830 --> 01:39:09.350
Now, if you excuse me, I have to get back to my date.
现在，失陪了，我得回去陪我的约会对象了。

1812
01:39:11.230 --> 01:39:13.910
There might be a lot of things about me that shock you.
关于我，可能会有很多让你震惊的事情。

1813
01:39:14.350 --> 01:39:19.550
And then I look him up and down, and I coyly kind of smile, and I walk away.
然后我上下打量了他一番，羞涩地笑了笑，转身走开了。

1814
01:39:21.890 --> 01:39:25.910
And now there's this series of scenes, right, that kind of wrap up the episode.
接下来是一系列场景，用来为这一集收尾。

1815
01:39:26.090 --> 01:39:27.790
There's a montage of Jan.
有一段关于简的蒙太奇。

1816
01:39:28.130 --> 01:39:29.710
She's trying to fix the Dundee.
她正试图修好那个邓迪奖杯。

1817
01:39:30.120 --> 01:39:32.230
You can tell she's sad.
看得出来她很伤心。

1818
01:39:32.530 --> 01:39:35.150
She knows this night went horrible.
她知道今晚过得一团糟。

1819
01:39:35.950 --> 01:39:39.810
Clearly knows this is a night they might not come back from, right?
很明显，她知道今晚过后，他们的关系可能就回不去了，对吧？

1820
01:39:40.350 --> 01:39:40.830
Yeah.
没错。

1821
01:39:41.150 --> 01:39:44.030
You see Jim and Pam having this really cute scene.
你看到吉姆和帕姆有一段非常可爱的戏。

1822
01:39:44.150 --> 01:39:45.190
They finally got food.
他们终于吃到东西了。

1823
01:39:45.370 --> 01:39:46.190
They're having a hamburger.
他们在吃汉堡。

1824
01:39:46.810 --> 01:39:47.290
Yes.
是的。

1825
01:39:47.470 --> 01:39:50.650
We got a fan question about this from Reagan Colliner,
我们收到了里根·科利纳发来的粉丝提问，

1826
01:39:50.690 --> 01:39:53.970
who wants to know what burger place did Jim and Pam eat at the end
她想知道吉姆和帕姆最后吃的是哪家的汉堡，

1827
01:39:53.970 --> 01:39:55.510
because the burgers looked amazing.
因为那些汉堡看起来太棒了。

1828
01:39:56.030 --> 01:39:58.070
I'll tell you what, the burgers were amazing.
我跟你说，那些汉堡确实很棒。

1829
01:39:58.250 --> 01:40:02.310
I don't know if it was just because I'd spent four days saying I was hungry,
我不知道是不是因为我连续四天都在喊饿，

1830
01:40:02.310 --> 01:40:06.030
but when I got that burger, I'm really eating it in that scene.
但当我拿到那个汉堡时，我在那场戏里是真的在吃。

1831
01:40:06.030 --> 01:40:07.190
I think you can tell.
我想你应该看得出来。

1832
01:40:07.190 --> 01:40:10.250
I think you were happy to eat anything other than that granola bar.
我觉得你当时能吃到除了燕麦棒以外的东西一定很开心。

1833
01:40:10.470 --> 01:40:11.710
I think I was.
我想是的。

1834
01:40:12.850 --> 01:40:18.710
Well, we filmed that scene at the Home Plate Burger joint,
我们是在“本垒打”汉堡店拍的那场戏，

1835
01:40:18.710 --> 01:40:21.770
and it was this little mom-and-pop hamburger stand,
那是一家很小的夫妻店，

1836
01:40:21.790 --> 01:40:24.110
which eventually, sadly, went out of business.
遗憾的是，后来倒闭了。

1837
01:40:24.110 --> 01:40:25.550
It's now a smog shop.
现在变成了一家汽车尾气检测店。

1838
01:40:25.750 --> 01:40:28.330
And in that same strip mall,
在同一个商业街区里，

1839
01:40:28.510 --> 01:40:33.910
there was a car wash that they turned into a Cold Stone Creamery,
原本有个洗车店，后来被改成了酷圣石冰淇淋店，

1840
01:40:33.910 --> 01:40:39.190
and that is where Andy and Angela are sitting in the car having their ice cream.
安迪和安吉拉就是在那里坐在车里吃冰淇淋的。

1841
01:40:39.190 --> 01:40:40.030
Yes.
没错。

1842
01:40:40.450 --> 01:40:43.110
Ed and I have a very funny story about this moment.
我和艾德关于那个瞬间有个非常有趣的段子。

1843
01:40:43.110 --> 01:40:44.390
And I asked Ed.
我问了艾德。

1844
01:40:44.490 --> 01:40:45.130
I texted him.
我给他发了短信。

1845
01:40:45.250 --> 01:40:48.450
I said, Ed, can I share about the car scene?
我说，艾德，我能分享一下车里那场戏的事吗？

1846
01:40:48.630 --> 01:40:53.010
And he's like, yes, you can tell everyone I farted in the car.
他说，可以，你可以告诉大家我在车里放屁了。

1847
01:40:53.990 --> 01:40:57.390
So we're in the car, and he's supposed to lick a little bit of my ice cream,
当时我们在车里，他本该舔一点我的冰淇淋，

1848
01:40:57.390 --> 01:40:59.830
and then I have to squish it on the side, right?
然后我得把它挤在边上，对吧？

1849
01:41:00.070 --> 01:41:03.490
It took a few tries to get that squish just right.
为了把那个挤压的动作拍好，我们拍了好几次。

1850
01:41:03.850 --> 01:41:06.530
And in between setting up, they'd have to clean the door,
在每次调整机位的时候，他们都得去擦车门，

1851
01:41:06.690 --> 01:41:10.270
and we're in between setups, and Ed had a little toot.
当时我们正在更换布景，埃德不小心放了个屁。

1852
01:41:11.210 --> 01:41:15.490
I was really pregnant, as you guys know, and it smelled.
你们都知道，我那时候怀孕了，所以味道特别重。

1853
01:41:15.730 --> 01:41:17.290
And I was like, oh, no, oh, no.
我当时心想，噢不，噢不。

1854
01:41:17.910 --> 01:41:20.210
And we were rolling when it happened.
事情发生的时候我们正在拍摄。

1855
01:41:20.370 --> 01:41:22.750
And so it's in the bloopers.
所以这段被收录进了花絮里。

1856
01:41:23.550 --> 01:41:24.530
